  "title": "England Moves Closer to Eliminating Hepatitis C",
  "summary": "A major public health milestone is within reach as England reports strong progress in diagnosing and treating hepatitis C, while health officials continue efforts to find people who remain unaware they carry the virus. England is moving closer to an important public health goal: eliminating hepatitis C as a major health threat. New figures show that significant progress has been made in recent years. More than 100,000 people in England have been diagnosed and treated for hepatitis C since 2015",
